WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
<v 0>Hey there! Here I'll talk you through rubric scripts,</v>

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:05.740
the place where your scripts get written, reviewed, and ready to record.

3
00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.140
It's basically one page for all your scripts so you're not digging through old

4
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.940
chats to find the one you wanted to record.

5
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.020
install prompt into your agent, then type slash rubric scripts and the page opens.

6
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.620
Then load your shortlist, the ideas you collected last week with slash latest and

7
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.940
slash outliers, or just run them again.

8
00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.440
Your agent then writes one for each idea with your slash script skill,

9
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.900
with three hook options from slash hooks,

10
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.160
in your own voice, from slash tone. Each script lands on the page

11
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:56.720
with its hook highlighted so you can see straight away if your first line

12
00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.180
grabs attention. If a line doesn't sound like you,

13
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.500
highlight any text and leave a comment on it,

14
00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:06.680
just like you would in a Google Doc. You'll also see a video area

15
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.740
and a channel area which will come back to in the content distribution modules.

16
00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:13.760
And once you've left your comments, copy them,

17
00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.280
send them to your agent, and you can do two things.

18
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.540
First, ask it to rewrite the scripts from your comments.

19
00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.180
Once one reads right, ask your agent to send it to wherever you read

20
00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.420
it while you record, like your telegram,

21
00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:31.000
or your own teleprompter. And don't wait for perfect,

22
00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.900
because volume is the game. Second,

23
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.820
with Teach My Tone Switched On, it also refines your slash tone skill from

24
00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:42.320
those same comments, so every script after this sounds a bit more like you.

25
00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.600
Now a few tips? Be specific in your comments.

26
00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.820
Instead of make this better, say,

27
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.800
this hook is too long, cut it to one line.

28
00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.060
Or just write what you'd actually say instead.

29
00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:01.100
In your own words, and read every script

30
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.860
out loud before you record it. If you stumble on a line,

31
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.640
that's the line to fix. Hope that was useful,

32
00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.440
and we'll see you in the next modules.
